Meeting Summary – AI-Powered Industrial Snag Reporting & Resolution System
Participants: Rachit Gupta and Farheen Fathima
Purpose: Discuss the proposed solution and working prototype for the Google AI Builder competition.
1. Project Overview
The idea is to build an AI-powered snag reporting and resolution platform for industries operating heavy machinery.
The platform will allow users to report machine issues (snags), document their history, and support the people responsible for resolving them.
Primary focus: Heavy machinery industries, including aviation, manufacturing, paper production, and other machinery-intensive sectors.
For the demo, the team plans to focus on two industries, with heavy machinery as the primary use case.
2. Proposed Application Workflow
Select Industry
Choose from a predefined dropdown
Select Machine
Search by manufacturer, name and model with autocomplete suggestions
Report Snag
Describe the issue and relevant machine history
AI-Generated Reporting Template
Generate fields based on industry and machine model
Resolution Workflow
Hand off the reported issue to the person responsible for fixing it

3. User Roles
Two profiles were proposed:
Role Responsibility
Snag Reporter Select industry and machine, enter issue details, and submit a snag report
Snag Resolver Handle and resolve reported machine issues
The detailed resolver workflow was not captured in the provided transcript.
4. Key Technical Requirements
- Industry selection: Predefined dropdown.
- Machine search: Google-like autocomplete, potentially using Elasticsearch-style search.
- Dynamic templates: AI-generated snag reporting forms customized to the selected industry and machine model.
- Issue history: Capture previous issues and relevant contextual information.
- Structured reporting: Support text fields and dropdowns to standardize issue submissions.
